      "text": "Let \\( f \\) be the function with \\( f(0) = 1 \\) and \\( f'(x) = \\frac{x^{2}}{1 + x^{3}} \\). Use a known Maclaurin series for \\( f' \\), integrated term by term, to find the sum of the first three nonzero terms of the Maclaurin series for \\( f \\)."
